DEVICE SPIKE

# Robot Lab: the crane lifts its hook, swings it a quarter turn, lets it down and swings back.
# Model: Crane. Motor A turns the turntable: an 8-tooth gear on the 28-tooth turntable, so
# 315 degrees of the motor are a quarter turn of the crane (90 x 28 / 8 = 315).
# Motor B turns the spindle of a small linear actuator one to one (360 degrees push 1.2 mm);
# the actuator pushes the boom up. 1800 degrees lift the boom from 30 to about 60 degrees,
# and the hook at its tip rises about 4 cm. The actuator holds the boom when B stops.
WHEN flag clicked:
  set motor stop action A hold
  set motor stop action B hold
  set motor speed A 10
  set motor speed B 100
  run motor B clockwise 1800 degrees
  wait 1 seconds
  run motor A clockwise 315 degrees
  wait 2 seconds
  run motor B counterclockwise 1800 degrees
  wait 1 seconds
  run motor A counterclockwise 315 degrees
